        "id": 10998,
        "name": "livingintruefreedom",
        "username": "livingintruefreedom",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/ec9cab/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-16T19:40:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I haven't seen a offical admin post on this yet. Maybe I didn't go deep enough into the ones that had 50 pages.</p><p>But first the wording of Wrest the Mind:<br>&nbsp;</p><p>Play this card next to a Target, other than a Hero or Villain Character Card. Whenever that target deals damage,<strong> you may</strong> redirect that damage to another target. <strong>If you do</strong>, <strong>The Visionary</strong> deals 3 psychic damage to that target and 3 psychic damage to <strong>herself</strong>.</p><p>If the target leaves play, destroy this card.</p><p>I bolded a few key words:</p><p>\"you may,\" so you don't have too.</p><p>\"If you do,\" Conditional reaction.</p><p>\"The Visionary\" &amp; \"herself\"</p><p>Basically the general arguement is does she take the damage if redirects and kills the target thus removing the card. I think the best way to view this is the order of operations.</p><p>Target: Electro-Pulse Bomb (Omintron device: 15HP).</p><p>Start of Villain turn. EPB does 15 damage to 4 heros.</p><p>Wrest the Mind is used to Redirect 15 damage to EPB<br>Conditional Reaction is activate:<br>15 damage to EPB<br>3 Damage to EPB<br>3 Damage to Visionary.<br>But there are two interupts. So the Order would be</p><p>15 Damage to EPB<br>Destroy EPB<br>Destroy Wrest the Mind<br>3 Damage to EPB (From The Visionary not the card as the card doesn't do the damage and The Visionary is still in play, also it is a Conditional Reaction so it happens because she did the action) Damage is ignored as the target is destroyed.<br>3 Damage to Visionary (as she is still in play and the damage is from a Conditional Reaction of her, and not damage from the card).</p><p>If I could get a Admin/Game designer to verify if this is correct that would be nice.<br>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:12.321Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
